<onlyinclude>'''Behavior''' refers to actions or patterns of activity of an organism or system in relation to internal and external conditions. In biology and psychology, examples include movement, communication, foraging, learning and deliberate inaction.

== Explanation ==
An animal may search for food, flee a predator or remain still when threatened. Researchers can observe these actions without assuming what the animal consciously experiences. Definitions vary across biology, psychology and engineering.

